cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "MSS Drum Fidelity Evaluation"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Ding
    given-names: Chuxin
    affiliation: "Universitat Autònoma de Barcelona"
    email: chuxinding@outlook.com
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0002-3508-4120"
repository-code: "https://github.com/dingchuxin/MSS_drum_fidelity_eval"
abstract: >-
  A reproducible pipeline for evaluating music source separation by the signal
  properties rhythm analysis depends on — onset timing, an eight-descriptor
  dynamic profile, and stem-labeling precision — alongside the field-standard
  BSS-Eval and SI-SDR metrics, on the MUSDB18-HQ test set.
keywords:
  - music source separation
  - music information retrieval
  - rhythm
  - microtiming
  - evaluation
  - MUSDB18
license: MIT
